# A transpose of 32-byte words by walk order alone: x is 8 rows of 16 words,
# y is 16 rows of 8 words. The destination walk is the iteration order; the
# source walk visits the same words column-first.
target ktpu.v9

fn transpose.l1(x: f16[8, 256] @dram, y: f16[16, 128] @dram)
    move
        copy w(x, (16, 32), (8, 512)) -> w(y, (16, 256), (8, 32))
